// Title: Renamed Schtasks Execution
// ID: f91e51c9-f344-4b32-969b-0b6f6b8537d4
// Status: experimental
// Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-11-27
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.persistence, attack.privilege-escalation, attack.stealth, attack.t1036.003, attack.t1053.005
// Description: Detects the execution of renamed schtasks.exe binary, which is a legitimate Windows utility used for scheduling tasks.
// One of the very common persistence techniques is schedule malicious tasks using schtasks.exe.
// Since, it is heavily abused, it is also heavily monitored by security products. To evade detection, threat actors may rename the schtasks.exe binary to schedule their malicious tasks.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((((process.command_line like "*_ /tn *" or process.command_line like "*_ /tr *" or process.command_line like "*_ /sc *" or process.command_line like "*_ /st *" or process.command_line like "*_ /ru *" or process.command_line like "*_ /fo *")) and ((process.command_line like "*_ /create *" or process.command_line like "*_ /delete *" or process.command_line like "*_ /query *" or process.command_line like "*_ /change *" or process.command_line like "*_ /run *" or process.command_line like "*_ /end *"))) and not ((process.command_line like "*_schtasks*")) and not (((process.command_line like "*_openfiles*" and process.command_line like "*_ /query *" and process.command_line like "*_ /fo*")))) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "schtasks.exe") and not ((process.executable endswith "\\schtasks.exe"))))
